{
 "text": " One man was struck by lightning seven times. He lived through every one. Roy Sullivan was a park ranger in the Virginia mountains. Your odds of being hit even once in a lifetime are about one in 15,000. In 1942, a bolt hit his fire lookout tower. It burned his leg and his big toe. 27 years later, it found him in his truck and burned off his eyebrows. The next summer, it hit him in his garden and seared his shoulder. Then it set his hair on fire three separate times. One strike knocked the shoe right off his foot. In 1977, he went fishing. Strike number seven burned his chest and stomach. Then a bear came for his fish and he hit it with a branch. Guinness still lists him as the person struck by lightning more times than anyone else on record. Subscribe for more Weird Humans!",
